# An unclosed parenthesis points back at the opening one.
mode: syntax
---- query
(from t | where (a > 1) | take 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..33
  PIPELINE@0..32
    PAREN_EXPR@0..32
      L_PAREN@0..1 "("
      PIPELINE@1..32
        IDENT@1..5 "from"
        WHITESPACE@5..6 " "
        NAME_REF@6..7
          IDENT@6..7 "t"
        WHITESPACE@7..8 " "
        PIPE@8..9 "|"
        WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
        WHERE_OP@10..23
          IDENT@10..15 "where"
          WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
          PAREN_EXPR@16..23
            L_PAREN@16..17 "("
            BIN_EXPR@17..22
              NAME_REF@17..18
                IDENT@17..18 "a"
              WHITESPACE@18..19 " "
              GT@19..20 ">"
              WHITESPACE@20..21 " "
              LITERAL@21..22
                LONG@21..22 "1"
            R_PAREN@22..23 ")"
        WHITESPACE@23..24 " "
        PIPE@24..25 "|"
        WHITESPACE@25..26 " "
        TAKE_OP@26..32
          IDENT@26..30 "take"
          WHITESPACE@30..31 " "
          LITERAL@31..32
            LONG@31..32 "5"
  WHITESPACE@32..33 "\n"

error[DS0112]: unclosed `(`
  --> query:1:1
  |
1 | (from t | where (a > 1) | take 5
  | ^                               - the input ends before a `)`
  | |
  | this `(` is never closed
  |
  = help: add `)` where the bracketed part ends
